<!-- Node naming rule (from the ISO, ISO/firstboot/set-hostname.sh):
     a node generated at first boot is `milady-<N>` with N random in
     10001..99999, five digits, stable width. The 1..10000 range is RESERVED for
     future NFT-mapped holder identities — a holder logs in to their own
     milady-<id> — so the public always draws from the upper range. A name you
     choose yourself is left alone; this node's operator reserved numbers for a
     private cluster, which is exactly the kind of exception the rule allows. -->
